WEBVTT

00:00:49.040 --> 00:00:50.070
Hodr...

00:00:51.700 --> 00:00:53.270
With just five units?

00:00:53.950 --> 00:00:57.080
I won't stop you,
but you'll be heading into enemy territory.

00:00:57.380 --> 00:00:58.830
I know.

00:00:58.830 --> 00:01:03.340
However, I believe it would be most effective for the Valkyrie Platoon

00:01:03.340 --> 00:01:08.080
to make a surprise attack on Binonten while you take on the Mizoram Stronghold here.

00:01:08.470 --> 00:01:10.130
I can come in from the north.

00:01:10.130 --> 00:01:13.330
There's a giant canyon in the northern wall.

00:01:13.870 --> 00:01:15.970
The Artemis can get through the canyon.

00:01:18.800 --> 00:01:21.870
I need to take down the wall as soon as possible.

00:01:22.190 --> 00:01:24.110
Yes, I understand.

00:01:25.070 --> 00:01:26.380
What are you doing?!

00:01:26.380 --> 00:01:27.610
Don't block my path!

00:01:34.590 --> 00:01:37.420
There isn't much time left, Hodr.

00:03:19.060 --> 00:03:20.970
Binonten, the capital of Krisna.

00:03:22.530 --> 00:03:26.570
They pride themselves on having mined the most amount of reactive quartz on the continent.

00:03:26.870 --> 00:03:30.320
And being in the middle of a great oasis, they are also blessed with fishing.

00:03:32.040 --> 00:03:37.450
A grave resource shortage was predicted in the neighboring Commonwealth of Athens

00:03:37.820 --> 00:03:40.580
and they began to invade the Krisna Kingdom.

00:03:42.000 --> 00:03:47.150
The General Heckel's platoon was in a stalemate at the Mizoram Stronghold,

00:03:47.150 --> 00:03:52.330
but Zess' Valkyrie Platoon utilized
the ability of their five Artemis units

00:03:52.330 --> 00:03:54.350
and launched a surprise attack on Binonten.

00:03:56.710 --> 00:03:59.850
Meanwhile, in Ilios, the capital of Athens,

00:03:59.850 --> 00:04:06.640
the executives were analyzing the
war under Secretary of War Loquis.

00:04:14.890 --> 00:04:25.850
In short, this excuse-filled report says that 150
Golems weren't enough to take down 50?

00:04:26.150 --> 00:04:29.780
We've already lost 2,000 soldiers.

00:04:29.780 --> 00:04:32.680
We can't possibly disclose this to the citizens.

00:04:32.680 --> 00:04:37.990
No, we can say that the soldiers were shot down
on their way back and received heavy injuries.

00:04:40.550 --> 00:04:42.900
Time is the real problem.

00:04:43.280 --> 00:04:48.620
If we spend any more time on the invasion,
Orlando may intervene.

00:04:49.150 --> 00:04:52.640
We'll have to dispatch General Borcuse at that point.

00:04:58.400 --> 00:05:02.360
H-However, Borcuse is...

00:05:05.210 --> 00:05:06.900
Please excuse me for interrupting in the middle of a meeting.

00:05:07.710 --> 00:05:12.240
I just received word that the Valkyrie Platoon is attacking Binonten

00:05:12.240 --> 00:05:15.040
under the command of General Ares' subordinate, Captain Zess.

00:05:15.520 --> 00:05:18.490
It seems like they left the western border three days ago

00:05:18.490 --> 00:05:21.180
to make a surprise attack on the capital.

00:05:22.420 --> 00:05:24.450
What an achievement.

00:05:24.450 --> 00:05:29.110
Zess broke through the northern canyon with the new Golems.

00:05:29.110 --> 00:05:31.300
Striking Binonten is a great feat.

00:05:31.710 --> 00:05:33.860
He is indeed the Secretary of War's younger brother.

00:05:33.860 --> 00:05:35.430
I'm impressed.

00:05:47.250 --> 00:05:49.690
<i>He acted on his own again...</i>

00:05:53.190 --> 00:05:56.790
<i>Zess, do you so strongly desire fame?</i>

00:06:04.470 --> 00:06:05.440
Listen up!

00:06:05.440 --> 00:06:07.320
I tell you this again and again:

00:06:07.710 --> 00:06:11.260
Our mission is to protect the capital!

00:06:11.700 --> 00:06:17.080
If you let an enemy inside, do not let them advance!

00:06:17.600 --> 00:06:18.630
Yes, Ma'am!

00:06:18.630 --> 00:06:21.190
Everyone get to your inner-wall defensive stations!

00:06:31.570 --> 00:06:34.700
Elza Squad, go cover the defense squad at the western gate!

00:06:35.090 --> 00:06:35.830
Sir!

00:06:36.560 --> 00:06:38.480
The rest of you, follow me.

00:06:38.480 --> 00:06:40.040
We'll defend the northern wall!

00:06:40.290 --> 00:06:41.210
Sir!

00:06:43.390 --> 00:06:47.070
General True's squad will sortie from the west!

00:06:47.070 --> 00:06:49.330
All units, come to the western gate!

00:06:52.310 --> 00:06:54.640
General True, please put that down!

00:06:55.220 --> 00:06:57.570
It's still in testing!

00:06:57.570 --> 00:06:58.850
General True!

00:06:59.220 --> 00:07:03.190
Exactly! I will go test it!

00:07:03.620 --> 00:07:04.630
I see.

00:07:04.630 --> 00:07:06.290
It's quite heavy.

00:07:13.990 --> 00:07:15.340
General True.

00:07:15.740 --> 00:07:18.280
Could you stay here this time?

00:07:18.930 --> 00:07:22.160
General Baldr, is that an order?

00:07:22.740 --> 00:07:23.720
Of course not.

00:07:24.210 --> 00:07:28.790
You, Imperial Guard General Sakura and I are all equal.

00:07:28.790 --> 00:07:30.100
Only His Highness can give us any orders.

00:07:30.580 --> 00:07:32.190
I was just making a suggestion.

00:07:32.870 --> 00:07:34.910
So you understand.

00:07:35.540 --> 00:07:38.380
Then I apologize, but I'll be ignoring your suggestion.

00:07:39.780 --> 00:07:44.410
The sword fits perfectly in the
heavy-lance sheath on my back.

00:07:44.410 --> 00:07:47.800
It must be itching to be used by me.

00:07:48.260 --> 00:07:49.690
General True!

00:07:49.690 --> 00:07:54.780
The Emperor called both you and I back here when General Sakura was already here.

00:07:55.100 --> 00:07:57.730
I believe he wishes to preserve our strengths.

00:07:57.730 --> 00:08:02.790
Your cowardice is precisely what has allowed our enemies to advance!

00:08:02.790 --> 00:08:06.590
My squad is heading out there to
protect the capital and its citizens!

00:08:20.570 --> 00:08:21.830
Three units damaged.

00:08:21.830 --> 00:08:22.860
Seventeen left.

00:08:24.350 --> 00:08:25.740
Can you draw them out?

00:08:25.980 --> 00:08:27.130
No.

00:08:27.130 --> 00:08:30.920
It appears they've been ordered not to engage fire.

00:08:31.410 --> 00:08:35.340
It was a perfectly executed surprise attack,
but they reacted surprisingly fast.

00:08:45.350 --> 00:08:46.990
Did the gate open?

00:08:48.340 --> 00:08:49.380
I'll take a look.

00:08:53.370 --> 00:08:54.800
I see one Golem.

00:08:54.800 --> 00:08:56.430
An unknown unit.

00:08:56.780 --> 00:08:58.120
Unknown?

00:08:58.120 --> 00:08:59.960
It's holding a red and white flag.

00:09:00.440 --> 00:09:01.310
A messenger?

00:09:03.720 --> 00:09:04.760
A signal?

00:09:05.470 --> 00:09:07.790
He seems to be requesting a negotiation.

00:09:07.790 --> 00:09:09.150
Operation...

00:09:10.370 --> 00:09:16.820
"Let's get Prince Bashful and the dull girl together"?

00:09:18.920 --> 00:09:20.120
Is that a code?

00:09:20.810 --> 00:09:22.390
I'll go negotiate.

00:09:22.940 --> 00:09:24.600
Captain Zess, that's too dangerous!

00:09:24.600 --> 00:09:25.580
I'll go too!

00:09:25.910 --> 00:09:27.290
Stay back, Erekt!

00:09:27.290 --> 00:09:29.640
I'll get both sides' units to retreat
until they're out of range.

00:09:33.030 --> 00:09:37.570
<i>Even during the Assam war, Zess always kept his cool.</i>

00:09:37.570 --> 00:09:39.490
<i>But he's flustered right now...</i>

00:09:40.400 --> 00:09:42.410
<i>Why are you here...</i>

00:09:43.310 --> 00:09:45.310
<i>when you don't like to fight?!</i>

00:10:06.870 --> 00:10:07.630
Who's there?

00:10:10.130 --> 00:10:11.740
If I recall correctly...

00:10:11.740 --> 00:10:13.250
You're the heir to the Tupel family.

00:10:13.890 --> 00:10:17.590
If you're a man from Athens,
why won't you fight one on one?

00:10:17.590 --> 00:10:18.760
Uh...

00:10:23.520 --> 00:10:26.180
And you're some... celebrity.

00:10:26.180 --> 00:10:28.040
Thanks.

00:10:28.040 --> 00:10:32.490
I don't like people who can only fight in groups,

00:10:33.040 --> 00:10:35.500
but I hate cowards even more.

00:10:36.320 --> 00:10:38.280
Would you fight back if it were one on one?

00:10:41.310 --> 00:10:42.530
I don't know.

00:10:42.940 --> 00:10:45.290
It's just something my dad taught me.

00:10:45.680 --> 00:10:47.800
If I can put up with it until they get bored,

00:10:47.800 --> 00:10:49.210
no one has to die.

00:10:49.210 --> 00:10:52.130
What if they hit you until you die?

00:10:52.450 --> 00:10:54.200
Would you still not fight?

00:10:56.960 --> 00:10:58.890
I haven't thought it out that far!

00:11:01.070 --> 00:11:04.240
<i>Does he have a spine or not?</i>

00:11:06.040 --> 00:11:07.290
Why did they jump you?

00:11:09.170 --> 00:11:10.390
So many questions.

00:11:10.390 --> 00:11:11.760
I don't know.

00:11:12.240 --> 00:11:14.320
It's because I'm different.

00:11:14.840 --> 00:11:16.320
<i>Different?</i>

00:11:17.050 --> 00:11:18.170
<i>So he's that guy?</i>

00:11:18.490 --> 00:11:19.060
Hey!

00:11:21.750 --> 00:11:26.650
If you stay within my ten maile radius,
I don't think anyone would pick a fight with you.

00:11:28.770 --> 00:11:33.110
Just don't get closer than three mailes.

00:11:34.220 --> 00:11:35.580
Not a bad deal, is it?

00:11:40.140 --> 00:11:41.710
I'm Zess.

00:11:54.980 --> 00:11:56.230
Rygart...

00:12:09.750 --> 00:12:11.040
It's been four years.

00:12:12.050 --> 00:12:15.720
But it looks like we don't have the time to celebrate our reunion.

00:12:16.750 --> 00:12:17.750
Rygart!

00:12:18.080 --> 00:12:19.140
Answer me!

00:12:19.140 --> 00:12:20.840
How are you moving that thing?

00:12:20.840 --> 00:12:23.860
Zess, my question comes first!

00:12:23.860 --> 00:12:26.760
Why are you invading Hodr's kingdom?!

00:12:27.170 --> 00:12:30.720
Athens has a very justifiable reason for this invasion.

00:12:31.100 --> 00:12:32.380
I can't stop it.

00:12:32.380 --> 00:12:33.840
Don't give me that!

00:12:33.840 --> 00:12:37.150
You've come this far into this kingdom! What's there to be justified about?

00:12:41.740 --> 00:12:44.330
General Baldr, they're not making any moves yet!

00:12:45.030 --> 00:12:50.220
As per Queen Sigyn's strong request,
we will be on standby for as long as we can!

00:12:51.330 --> 00:12:54.510
The real problem is General True
who went to the western gate.

00:12:59.470 --> 00:13:02.420
Our enemy has attacked from the north.

00:13:02.420 --> 00:13:03.910
We'll surround them and destroy them!

00:13:04.860 --> 00:13:09.050
We Draupnir Heavy Knights strike
like lightning and adapt like water.

00:13:09.050 --> 00:13:10.300
Charge!

00:13:10.300 --> 00:13:11.740
Run!

00:13:11.740 --> 00:13:12.850
Roger, Sir!

00:13:30.000 --> 00:13:30.970
Look!

00:13:31.550 --> 00:13:35.500
This war was originally triggered by Orlando in the east.

00:13:36.340 --> 00:13:40.680
They were secretly communicating with the soldiers who started the war in Assam.

00:13:41.280 --> 00:13:45.990
What's worse, Krisna allowed the Orlando Army

00:13:45.990 --> 00:13:48.980
to advance through Krisnan lands to take part in the war.

00:13:50.190 --> 00:13:55.850
In short, Krisna helped Orlando in their ambitions.

00:13:56.230 --> 00:13:57.320
Helped?!

00:13:57.870 --> 00:13:59.400
W-Wait a minute!

00:13:59.400 --> 00:14:02.440
Do you seriously think Hodr has any ambitions?!

00:14:02.440 --> 00:14:04.550
Of course not!

00:14:04.550 --> 00:14:07.910
I know very well that he doesn't even care about the throne!

00:14:08.370 --> 00:14:12.360
Orlando took advantage of their
international military training with Krisna

00:14:12.360 --> 00:14:13.870
to travel through their territory.

00:14:14.520 --> 00:14:15.890
Hodr was set up!

00:14:18.990 --> 00:14:20.330
Please, Rygart!

00:14:20.680 --> 00:14:23.420
Knock some sense into him and make him surrender!

00:14:23.910 --> 00:14:25.440
You should be able to do that!

00:14:25.720 --> 00:14:28.090
I can't just agree with that!

00:14:28.090 --> 00:14:31.550
You need to retreat and tell Athens to stop the invasion!

00:14:31.940 --> 00:14:33.390
That's the proper way to settle this!

00:14:34.240 --> 00:14:36.530
I'm still only 25.

00:14:36.530 --> 00:14:38.740
I don't have the authority to do that.

00:14:39.210 --> 00:14:45.060
We can't always be stupid students who
simply voice our ideals and reasons.

00:14:45.660 --> 00:14:50.320
Unfortunately, once a war starts,
it won't end until it's settled.

00:14:50.320 --> 00:14:52.240
I can't accept those conditions.

00:14:52.650 --> 00:14:53.770
Conditions?

00:15:00.970 --> 00:15:03.710
<i>The enemy... is getting ready from the west?</i>

00:15:04.390 --> 00:15:08.120
<i>Rygart, you were just used to buy them time.</i>

00:15:08.460 --> 00:15:11.280
Zess, are you saying that knowing the conditions—

00:15:12.040 --> 00:15:12.820
Hey!

00:15:15.300 --> 00:15:16.650
Listen up, Rygart!

00:15:17.100 --> 00:15:19.600
The fall of Krisna is already set in stone!

00:15:20.030 --> 00:15:23.200
The question is whether it's now or later!

00:15:23.940 --> 00:15:25.100
He's aiming his gun!

00:15:25.490 --> 00:15:26.860
General Baldr!

00:15:29.270 --> 00:15:30.690
I'll count to five.

00:15:30.690 --> 00:15:35.080
Go back and make Hodr surrender or fight here!

00:15:35.080 --> 00:15:40.140
General Borcuse is going to be dispatched for the
second invasion. He's a merciless master of war.

00:15:40.510 --> 00:15:43.060
He'll attack with over 200 units!

00:15:43.790 --> 00:15:45.540
There's no time!

00:15:45.540 --> 00:15:48.480
Stop resisting and surrender!

00:15:49.590 --> 00:15:50.330
<i>Zess...</i>

00:15:50.960 --> 00:15:52.030
I'm starting.

00:15:52.550 --> 00:15:53.220
One!

00:15:56.020 --> 00:15:57.800
15 units all at once.

00:15:58.130 --> 00:15:59.940
Krisna sure has resources to spare.

00:16:01.410 --> 00:16:02.880
I'm so nervous.

00:16:02.880 --> 00:16:04.610
You have no reason to be.

00:16:04.870 --> 00:16:07.870
You're not gonna hit a single enemy.

00:16:09.180 --> 00:16:10.660
I've hit something once!

00:16:12.640 --> 00:16:13.710
Two!

00:16:13.710 --> 00:16:16.250
<i>Zess, you won't fire.</i>

00:16:22.180 --> 00:16:23.680
Fish at the west, huh?

00:16:24.430 --> 00:16:26.150
You're a genius, Zess!

00:16:26.150 --> 00:16:27.510
I'm fishing tons!

00:16:28.620 --> 00:16:29.570
Three!

00:16:31.490 --> 00:16:33.080
<i>You of all people would back away.</i>

00:16:33.080 --> 00:16:33.980
<i>Go back!</i>

00:16:33.980 --> 00:16:35.940
<i>Go back and convince Hodr!</i>

00:16:38.870 --> 00:16:40.300
<i>You can't shoot.</i>

00:16:40.300 --> 00:16:43.190
<i>You know you're wrong.</i>

00:16:44.190 --> 00:16:46.260
<i>Why won't you retreat, Rygart?</i>

00:16:46.910 --> 00:16:47.810
Four!

00:16:53.440 --> 00:16:54.360
Five!

00:16:54.360 --> 00:16:55.670
Rygart!

00:17:12.770 --> 00:17:14.450
<i>Idiot, don't move!</i>

00:17:14.450 --> 00:17:15.450
<i>I don't want to kill you!</i>

00:17:17.580 --> 00:17:19.050
Stop!

00:17:24.060 --> 00:17:25.370
It's fast!

00:17:25.800 --> 00:17:28.920
How can that black thing accelerate so fast?

00:17:29.160 --> 00:17:30.150
Captain Zess!

00:17:30.150 --> 00:17:31.780
I'll overtake him from the front!

00:17:31.780 --> 00:17:33.120
Wait, Erekt!

00:17:33.520 --> 00:17:35.980
Open the gate! Charge!

00:17:40.900 --> 00:17:41.940
Erekt.

00:17:41.940 --> 00:17:42.900
Their real army is coming.

00:17:43.260 --> 00:17:44.700
He doesn't have a weapon.

00:17:44.700 --> 00:17:45.620
Leave him be!

00:17:45.990 --> 00:17:47.040
Okay!

00:17:47.920 --> 00:17:51.970
Private Dan, cover for the black Golem!

00:17:51.970 --> 00:17:52.700
Yes, sir!

00:17:54.240 --> 00:17:56.600
<i>If I recall correctly, he's some man named Rygart</i>

00:17:56.600 --> 00:18:00.040
<i>who was personally welcomed by
General Baldr and His Highness.</i>

00:18:02.850 --> 00:18:04.560
<i>Is he confused?</i>

00:18:04.560 --> 00:18:06.090
<i>How far does he plan to go?</i>

00:18:06.090 --> 00:18:07.760
<i>And he's fast!</i>

00:18:15.960 --> 00:18:18.050
Damn, we've lost six.

00:18:19.050 --> 00:18:20.710
This is a terrible location.

00:18:20.710 --> 00:18:22.340
We're completely overpowered.

00:18:25.600 --> 00:18:26.690
General True!

00:18:27.440 --> 00:18:28.600
We should retreat!

00:18:28.870 --> 00:18:30.320
Give me a break!

00:18:30.320 --> 00:18:32.760
They only have three units!

00:18:32.760 --> 00:18:35.060
If we can get the upperhand,
we'll turn this game around!

00:18:35.060 --> 00:18:38.480
They're too high up for our Golems!

00:18:39.720 --> 00:18:41.840
At this rate, we'll be annihilated!

00:18:49.200 --> 00:18:52.120
Like hell I can back down here!

00:18:52.120 --> 00:18:54.570
Cleo, at least land one shot!

00:18:54.570 --> 00:18:56.570
You're so incompetent!

00:18:56.570 --> 00:18:58.140
Okay!

00:19:03.730 --> 00:19:04.550
I got one!

00:19:04.760 --> 00:19:05.990
Fall back!

00:19:05.990 --> 00:19:07.940
I'll hold them back!

00:19:07.940 --> 00:19:11.110
Survive and inherit my will!

00:19:11.110 --> 00:19:12.640
Protect the capital!

00:19:14.400 --> 00:19:15.920
What are you saying?

00:19:15.920 --> 00:19:19.770
If you don't retreat, we aren't allowed to retreat!

00:19:21.070 --> 00:19:23.390
Retreat!

00:19:25.320 --> 00:19:27.800
Okay, they're starting to move back.

00:19:27.800 --> 00:19:28.830
Follow them!

00:19:29.150 --> 00:19:30.800
I'll obliterate them!

00:19:30.800 --> 00:19:32.550
<i>Please retreat safely.</i>

00:19:36.550 --> 00:19:38.500
Queen Sigyn, please come to your senses!

00:19:38.970 --> 00:19:40.860
Please come back to the castle!

00:19:46.180 --> 00:19:47.640
He shot at me.

00:19:48.340 --> 00:19:51.480
Zess, you asshole.

00:19:51.480 --> 00:19:53.410
Should I hide here for a while?

00:19:53.930 --> 00:19:56.320
No, if I abandon this...

00:19:58.400 --> 00:20:00.650
Why's this a different color?

00:20:00.650 --> 00:20:03.170
Translate into my language, dammit.

00:20:04.250 --> 00:20:06.370
I can read the number.

00:20:06.370 --> 00:20:07.270
Five?

00:20:13.650 --> 00:20:14.650
You!

00:20:14.980 --> 00:20:18.940
You ruined my chance to capture the king!

00:20:31.580 --> 00:20:33.220
<i>What the...?</i>

00:20:35.030 --> 00:20:38.110
<i>How is it... so high?</i>

00:20:50.810 --> 00:20:52.700
<i>What the hell was that?</i>

00:20:52.700 --> 00:20:55.080
<i>It landed without an empennage to slow it down?</i>

00:20:55.530 --> 00:20:58.700
<i>No, the notable thing is that height!</i>

00:20:59.060 --> 00:21:01.030
<i>If they were to mass produce this...</i>

00:21:02.580 --> 00:21:05.910
<i>They'd easily overtake our capital's final defensive line!</i>

00:21:07.250 --> 00:21:09.720
I have to finish you, here and now!

00:21:12.020 --> 00:21:14.090
I'll break you into a thousand pieces!

00:21:18.100 --> 00:21:20.880
<i>He's only wearing a makeshift light armor...</i>

00:21:21.260 --> 00:21:22.430
<i>Rygart...</i>

00:21:27.870 --> 00:21:29.140
I know that damaged him.

00:21:30.460 --> 00:21:33.070
I hit him at least four times.

00:21:36.600 --> 00:21:39.820
T-That wasn't as tough as I thought.

00:21:40.430 --> 00:21:43.320
I should at least report this to Zess later.

00:22:06.690 --> 00:22:08.270
H-He's still standing!

00:22:08.610 --> 00:22:10.480
Holding that claymore with a single arm!

00:23:51.350 --> 00:23:54.480
I was running as fast as I could to save my life.

00:23:55.550 --> 00:23:58.850
Close combat, close quarter battle.
